{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2619","id":2534773721,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz886XFZPZ","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2619","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2619.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2619.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2619","number":2619,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Tags: reimplement, make first class","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR is going to be the core work of #2417, redoing our Tags support.\r\n\r\nFrom the [tailscale docs](https://tailscale.com/kb/1068/tags):\r\n> Tailscale tags are how you authenticate and identify non-user devices, such as servers and [ephemeral nodes](https://tailscale.com/kb/1111/ephemeral-nodes). They serve two primary purposes: to provide an identity to non-user devices and to let you manage [access control policies](https://tailscale.com/kb/1393/access-control) based on purpose. In this context, a purpose could be anything from hosting a web server to serving as a [subnet router](https://tailscale.com/kb/1019/subnets) for employees in a specific geographic location.\r\n\r\nWe do not really implement tags this way, as a node is _always_ associated with a user, even if it is tagged.\r\n\r\nAfter this PR, we will stream line tags to work in the same way as upstream, and making sure we align and ensure that tagged devices are truly not associated with a user.\r\n\r\nThis is an important building block to ensure that the Tags part of the Policy works in the correct way and provide the correct isolation.","created_at":"2025-05-21T15:29:33Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T11:15:59Z","closed_at":"2025-11-28T11:15:59Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/milestones/13","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/milestone/13","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/milestones/13/labels","id":13296438,"node_id":"MI_kwDOEFLz884AyuM2","number":13,"title":"v0.28.0","description":"Tags","creator":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"pub